SPDX / provenance boundary (scope note — not part of the MIT license text above)
- The MIT license above applies to **original scaffold code written for this
  repository only** (see ATTRIBUTION.md "Original scaffold (this repository)" and
  the per-file table in PROVENANCE.md).
- It does **not** re-license: EchoCLIP prompt strings or any upstream-aligned
  logic (`echoclip/prompts.py`, `echoclip/official_parity.py`,
  `echoclip/preprocess.py`); official hub weights
  (`hf-hub:mkaichristensen/echo-clip`); Stanford AIMI / EchoNet dataset terms; or
  third-party packages listed in the requirements files.
- Neither the official EchoCLIP weights nor EchoNet-Dynamic data are redistributed
  in this repository; obtain them under their own upstream terms
  (docs/OBTAIN_DATA_AND_WEIGHTS.md).
- `echoclip/text.py` is an independently authored report
  normalizer whose behavior intentionally overlaps upstream EchoCLIP report cleaning;
  no upstream code is vendored or line-copied in this repository, and whether the
  upstream echonet/echo_CLIP utils.py source was consulted is **unclear — needs
  author confirmation** (canonical wording; see PROVENANCE.md).
- File-level provenance: ATTRIBUTION.md and PROVENANCE.md. This scope note is an
  engineering statement, not legal advice; a per-file provenance audit with the
  author's institution is recommended before submission.
